{"causes": ["The system of prince-bishoprics within the Holy Roman Empire provided a framework for ecclesiastical leaders to hold significant temporal power.", "The political fragmentation of late medieval Germany necessitated strong regional leaders capable of maintaining order and defending their territories.", "The ongoing need for clerical reform and administrative efficiency within German dioceses created opportunities for proactive bishops to implement changes."], "effects": ["Heinrich Groß von Trockau's reign strengthened the administrative and financial stability of the Prince-Bishopric of Bamberg.", "His patronage led to significant architectural developments and fortifications within the city of Bamberg, enhancing its prestige and defenses.", "The consolidation of power under his leadership contributed to Bamberg's continued role as an important ecclesiastical and political center in Franconia."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "prince-bishopric-of-bamberg", "sourceName": "Prince-Bishopric of Bamberg", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "heinrich-gro-von-trockau", "targetName": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau", "context": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau served as the Prince-Bishop of Bamberg from 1487 to 1501, governing its temporal and spiritual affairs."}, {"sourceSlug": "holy-roman-empire", "sourceName": "Holy Roman Empire", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "heinrich-gro-von-trockau", "targetName": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau", "context": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau's entire life and episcopate took place within the political and cultural context of the Holy Roman Empire."}, {"sourceSlug": "bamberg", "sourceName": "Bamberg", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "heinrich-gro-von-trockau", "targetName": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau", "context": "Heinrich Groß von Trockau resided and conducted the majority of his episcopal duties in Bamberg, the seat of his prince-bishopric."}, {"sourceSlug": "maximilian-i", "sourceName": "Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor", "verb"